)ATTR DEFAULT(@}_)
 @ TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(WHITE)
 } TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(GREEN)
 { TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(TURQ)
 _ TYPE(INPUT)  INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(RED)    CAPS(ON) JUST(LEFT)
 ! TYPE(OUTPUT) INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(YELLOW) CAPS(OFF) JUST(LEFT)
)BODY
@HELP: Status Panel -- Commands                 !ISFHMSG                      }
@COMMAND INPUT ===>_ISFHCMD                                                  }
}
}  Besides the commands you can give on every panel (topic 12 of the
}  contents), the Status panel takes:
}
{  ?                }The further fields of the jobs, and back (topic 4).
{  ST [name]        }The list again, with other classes or another name.
{  Enter            }With an empty command line: the list read again, to
}                   show what has changed.
{  UP, DOWN         }Scroll by the amount in the SCROLL field (PAGE, HALF,
}                   CSR, DATA, a number of lines, or MAX on the key).
{  TOP, BOTTOM      }To the first or last job.
{  FIND string      }The next job whose line holds the string goes to the
}                   top; PF5 (RFIND) finds the next one.
{  LOCATE n         }The job in row n goes to the top.
{  RIGHT, LEFT      }With ?: move the further fields (PF11, PF10).
{  END              }Back to the menu.
}
}  The other panel commands (DA, I, O, H, PR, INIT, LOG) go to that panel.
}
}  PF7: Status panel help   PF10: back   PF3: back to SDSF
)PROC
  &ISFHPFK = .PFKEY
  &ZUP = ISFHST
)END
